From: Lithify <lithify@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] core: say when the access point stops answering the keep-alive

librespot shuts the session down when a Ping or PongAck does not come in time, and returns
the error from the dispatch task, whose result nothing logs: the session ends without a word
while spirc, idle, stays parked on it. Log it where it is noticed, so that a watchdog can tell
(Lithify's agent restarts librespot then).

---
diff --git a/core/src/session.rs b/core/src/session.rs
index 333678f..4c7d4fc 100644
--- a/core/src/session.rs
+++ b/core/src/session.rs
@@ -926,6 +926,11 @@ where
         if let Poll::Ready(()) = this.timeout.as_mut().poll(cx) {
             match this.keep_alive_state {
                 ExpectingPing | ExpectingPongAck => {
+                    // Said here: the task's error is not logged where it ends.
+                    error!(
+                        "session lost connection to server ({:?})",
+                        this.keep_alive_state
+                    );
                     if !session.is_invalid() {
                         session.shutdown();
                     }
